## Details

### Base URL

\`https://api.acmeweather.example/v2\`

**Status:** Documented
> "All requests are made to https://api.acmeweather.example/v2"
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/](https://docs.acmeweather.example/)

### Authentication (primary)

- Type: api_key
- Location: header
- Parameter: \`X-Api-Key\`
- API key in the X-Api-Key header

**Status:** Documented
> "sending your API key in the X-Api-Key header"
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/](https://docs.acmeweather.example/)

### Authentication alternatives

Other methods the docs state. Each has a sample request in the Postman "Auth alternatives" folder.

#### 1. basic in header (Authorization)

- Type: basic
- Location: header
- Parameter: \`Authorization\`
- HTTP Basic with the API key as username

**Status:** Documented
> "HTTP Basic authentication, with the API key as the username and an empty password"
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/](https://docs.acmeweather.example/)

#### 2. api_key in query (api_key)

- Type: api_key
- Location: query
- Parameter: \`api_key\`
- API key as the api_key query parameter

**Status:** Documented
> "may pass the key as the api_key query parameter instead"
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/](https://docs.acmeweather.example/)

### Endpoints

| Method | Path | Purpose | Key params | Status | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| GET | \`/forecast\` | 7-day forecast for a city | \`city\` (query, required), \`units\` (query) | Documented | [/endpoints](https://docs.acmeweather.example/endpoints) |
| GET | \`/locations\` | List saved locations | \`cursor\` (query) | Documented | [/endpoints](https://docs.acmeweather.example/endpoints) |
| GET | \`/locations/{id}\` | Saved location details | \`id\` (path, required) | Documented | [/endpoints](https://docs.acmeweather.example/endpoints) |
| POST | \`/alerts\` | Subscribe to severe-weather alerts | \`location_id\` (body, required), \`callback_url\` (body, required) | Inferred | [/endpoints](https://docs.acmeweather.example/endpoints) |

### Pagination

- Style: cursor
- Parameters: \`cursor\`, \`limit\`
- Pass next_cursor as cursor

**Status:** Documented
> "pass the cursor value from the previous response's next_cursor field"
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/endpoints](https://docs.acmeweather.example/endpoints)

### Rate limits

- Limits: 60 requests per minute per key
- Headers: \`X-RateLimit-Remaining\`, \`X-RateLimit-Reset\`
- HTTP 429 when exceeded

**Status:** Documented
> "Each API key may make 60 requests per minute."
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/rate-limits](https://docs.acmeweather.example/rate-limits)

### Webhooks

- Supported: yes
- Events: \`alert.triggered\`, \`alert.cleared\`
- Signature verification: HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body in X-Acme-Signature
- POST to callback_url

**Status:** Documented
> "an HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body, signed with your webhook secret"
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/webhooks](https://docs.acmeweather.example/webhooks)

### Error format

JSON error object with code and message

\`\`\`json
{ "error": { "code": "invalid_city", "message": "City not found" } }
\`\`\`

**Status:** Documented
> "Errors use standard HTTP status codes and a JSON body"
> — [https://docs.acmeweather.example/](https://docs.acmeweather.example/)

### Versioning

- Scheme: url_path
- Current: v2
- Major version in the path

**Status:** Inferred
